Another one I found on main:
```
d = {}

class X(object):
    def __hash__(self):
        return 1
    def __eq__(self, other):
        d.clear()

d[X()] = None
d[X()] = None
for _ in range(10):
    d.pop(X(), None)

```
It is aborted with `Assertion failed: PyUnicode_CheckExact(ep->me_key), file X:\Work\cpython\main\Objects\dictobject.c, line 1048`
